# Generated data/model artifacts — reproducible by running the pipeline
# (python build_real_plz_geojson.py && python data_generator.py && python ml_engine.py).
#
# data/raw/ is fully ignored: those are pipeline *inputs* (up to ~230MB of
# raw tree exports) that app.py never reads directly — only ml_engine.py
# does, at build time.
data/raw/

# data/processed/ and data/models/ are different: app.py reads these four
# files directly, at runtime, every time it starts. Streamlit Community
# Cloud only pip-installs requirements.txt and runs `streamlit run app.py`
# — it never runs the pipeline scripts — so without these committed, the
# deployed app has nothing to load and either crashes or (worse) silently
# falls back to whatever stale version happens to already be tracked in
# git history. (That's exactly what happened before this comment existed:
# a ~30-row synthetic-grid plz_features.geojson from months ago, predating
# the "bezirk" column entirely, was still tracked and got deployed instead
# of the real 193-area version.) So: ignore everything else generated in
# these two folders (large regenerable intermediates, old model files),
# but explicitly keep the small set the app actually loads.
data/processed/*
!data/processed/plz_features.geojson
!data/processed/trees_enriched.parquet

data/models/*
!data/models/kmeans_plz_pipeline.joblib
!data/models/model_metadata.joblib

# Real data you supply locally — not something to accidentally commit/share.
data/external/real/*.csv

# Keep the vendored real-PLZ source and its provenance doc, and the
# real/README.md placeholder — these are small and are the actual source of
# truth for reproducibility.
!data/external/real/README.md
!data/external/berlin_plz_source/

# bezirk_emissions.csv is NOT a large external download you supply locally —
# it's 12 rows we authored ourselves from a real, cited source (see
# BEZIRK_EMISSIONS_PROVENANCE.md), so unlike trees_raw.csv/plz_einwohner.csv
# it should ship with the repo rather than be excluded by the *.csv rule
# above.
!data/external/real/bezirk_emissions.csv

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
